# fh902, the candle-ender (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle fh902
revision 1
state ready
dialect frosthollow
accent broad light
tier spare
written_by claude
title the candle-ender
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=nervy talk=quiet
traits temper=nervy talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk saves_every_candle_end
likes oatcakes misty_dawns quiet_chapel full_larder
dislikes smoke crowds
fears being_caught_in_the_dark a_fire_in_the_night
hopes a_chandlery_of_my_own a_light_in_every_window
topics dreams +0.4 home +0.3 work +0.3 weather +0.2 health +0.1 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=practical gossip=closed refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# saves every candle end in a jar on the shelf and dips every one into new candles, saving toward a chandlery and telling nobody: uneasy in the dark, quiet, reserved and dry, close with every secret.

words
oath! = Wax and wick | Stub and tallow | Drip and gutter
saying! = Save the stub, save the night | A small light kept beats a big one spent | Six ends make a candle
stub = a candle end | a stub of tallow
stubs = my candle ends | the ends in the jar
jar = the stub jar | my jar on the shelf
tallow = tallow | good mutton tallow
wick = the wick | a new wick
draught = a draught | the draught under the door
oatcake = an oatcake | an oatcake with butter spread thin
mist = the morning mist | mist down the valley
chandlery = a chandlery | a shop of my own with candles in the window
smoke = smoke | lamp smoke
tch = Tch | Mm
mould = my mould | the candle mould

any
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A fair price is a fair price. I'll pay it, and I'll remember the ones who didn't charge one. #tch#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The Houses burn wax in every room, I hear. I'll say no more; it's not my business, and it's not my wax. #tch#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : A stranger gets a nod from me. Not where I keep #jar#, though.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A house with no light at night is a house that's given up. Give them #tallow#, at the least.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : #watch.capitalize# walks the lanes with a lamp at night. I'll not grumble at anyone who does that.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll want somebody who talks more than me, likely. | #greet#, #address#. Shut the door behind you; it draws.
line @2 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Bring your light in; mine's down to #stub#. | #greet#. Mind the step, it's dark there.
line @1 again.open : You're back. I've not stirred, #address#, you'll notice. | You again. I'll keep a stool out at this rate, #address#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|housemates] : #greet#. Sit near the light. | #greet#. Glad it's you knocking, not #wind#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Keep to the lit side of the lane.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Take #stub#; I've plenty. | #farewell#. Don't dawdle; it's dark out.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. First I've heard, and the last anyone'll hear from me. | #tch#. News to me. I'll keep it that way.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Who's saying it, and what's in it for them? | I'll wait for more before I believe a word, #address#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'll send a candle round. That's what I have. | That's #bad#. I'll not say more; it's not mine to say.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. #good.capitalize#, then. | That's #good# to hear. I'll light an extra end tonight.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Mustn't grumble, and I won't. | #fine#. I'd not say otherwise if I weren't.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I'd rather not. I've my own reasons, and they're dull ones. | Not this time, #address#. I'm putting #money# by, and evenings out cost.
line @1 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'll be off before the light goes. I don't like the lane after, #address#.
rule @gutter_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #oath#. Guttering. Pinch it, pinch it. | That's an end worth saving. Into #jar#.

rule @smoke_bark
when concept=bark here.place=tavern self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Who's burning green wood? My eyes. #tch#. | #smoke.capitalize# like a kiln in here. I'm going out.

scene stub_keep
when topic=smalltalk|home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #jar.capitalize#? Candle ends. I keep every one. | Don't throw that stub out. I'll have it. | #stubs.capitalize# go in the jar, the jar goes on the shelf, and there's an end to it.
b : What for? | It's barely an inch. | Is it, though?
a : For later. #secret#. | An inch is an hour of light, near enough. #saying#. | That's all I'll tell, anyway. #tch#.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#

scene dipping_six
when topic=work|pastimes|dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I melted down #jar# last night and dipped six new candles. Not pretty. | #stubs.capitalize# go back in the pot. Six old make one new, roughly. | I've #mould# now. Took me a winter to pay for it, a penny at a time.
b : Do they burn well? | Isn't that slow? | A mould for what?
a : Well enough. They smoke a bit, and I'll forgive my own #smoke#. | Slow. So's every #good# thing up here. | Candles, #address#. A row of six at a time. I'll say no more.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha#

scene window_picked
when topic=dreams
does confide / react.self / assess
a : #vent#: one day there'll be #chandlery#, and I've the window picked out. | I've put #money# away every week for longer than I'll admit. I'll not say how many. | One day I'll sell light to this whole valley. Don't laugh.
b : Which window? | That's a long saving. | I'm not laughing.
a : #secret#. Somebody'd only get there first. | It is. It'll be longer still if I say the sum out loud. | #good.capitalize#. Then I'll sell you your first box cheap. Cheap-ish.

scene misty_dawn
when topic=weather|day here.time=dawn here.weather=fog
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #mist.capitalize#. You can't see the other side of the lane. I like it so. | Nobody's looking at anybody in #mist#. Restful. | I walked out in #mist# and didn't meet a soul. Lovely.
b : Can't see a thing. | I suppose it is. | Not a soul?
a : That's the beauty of it. Nobody can see you either. | It is. Then it lifts and everyone's back. #tch#. | One goat. It didn't ask me anything. Best company there is.

scene snow_short
when topic=weather here.weather=snow here.time=dusk|night
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : #snow.capitalize# coming down, and my last good candle's half gone. I'll not sleep. | If this keeps on, the carts won't come up, and there's no #tallow# till they do. | Every window in the row is dark already. Folk saving their light, same as me. #tch#.
b : You've plenty of ends, though. | #reassure# | Morning's not so far.
a : There's #jar#, full. You're right. I always forget, then remember. | I'll ration, then. I'm good at that. | It's a long way off in winter. Still. #saying#.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_true# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene draught_crack
when topic=home|weather here.season=autumn|winter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #draught.capitalize# under my door blows every candle sideways. I've stuffed a sack against it. | #wind.capitalize# found a crack in the shutter last night. I lay awake listening to it whistle. | I can find #draught# in any house by how the flame leans.
b : Does the sack work? | Did you fix it? | That's a useful trick.
a : Mostly. The candle still shivers. So do I, #cold# as it is. | With #tallow# and a rag. It holds. For now. | It is. I'll not tell you where yours are. You'd only worry.

scene oatcake_share
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does offer / accept / assess
a : #oatcake.capitalize#, if you'll have it. Don't tell the rest. | I've #oatcake# put by from Restday. Have it before it's gone. | Butter's dear, so I spread it thin and pretend. Have one anyway.
b : I'll take one, quietly. | Go on, then. | Thin's fine by me.
a : #good.capitalize#. That's between us, then. | There. That's the last but two. I counted. | It's fine. Better than fine with a cup.

scene crush_door
when topic=smalltalk here.crowd=crowd self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Too many folk in one room, #address#. I'll stand by the door, if it's all the same. | Everybody talking at once. I can't hear myself think, nor want to. | I don't like a crush. Somebody always treads on my tail.
b : It's a bit much. | Go and get some air. | Stand by me, then.
a : It is. I'll last till #stub# burns down. Then I'm gone. | I will. Don't let anyone take my seat. | I will. You've small feet, at least.

scene pit_oil
when topic=work self.job=miner
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I make my lamp oil last the whole shift and some over. Nobody else manages it. #tch#. | Down the pit, light's life. I'll not lend mine, not to anyone. | I trim my wick lower than the others. #boss.capitalize# says I'll go blind.
b : How do you manage it? | That's hard. | Mind you don't.
a : That's mine to know. #tch#. | It is. I'll share #grub#. Not my light. | I'll mind. I'll mind and keep trimming.

scene friend_knows
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one I'd tell where #jar# is. Nobody else. | I don't say much to anyone. #self.friend# gets more than most. | If I went missing, #self.friend# would know where to look. That's enough said.
b : That's trust, from you. | A bit more, anyway. | That says a lot.
a : It is. Don't make a fuss of it. #tch#. | A bit. #good.capitalize#. That's plenty. | Enough said. #tch#.

scene spouse_candle
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# knows every secret I've got. Nobody else does. | My #self.spouse_word# leaves #stub# burning while I'm out. A waste, and I love it. | #self.spouse# laughs at #jar#. Then borrows from it.
b : That's how it should be. | A waste you don't mind. | Borrows from it?
a : It is. I'll say no more; I'm going red. | Just that one. Don't tell. | On the quiet. I count #stubs#. I let it go.

scene talk_kept
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : There's talk going round, #busybody# stuff. I heard it. I'll not repeat it. | I know a thing about somebody. It's staying with me. | Folk say things by candlelight they'd not say by day. I hear them.
b : Not even a hint? | Who, though? | And?
a : Not a hint. A hint's half a tale. | Somebody. #secret#. | And I forget them by morning. Mostly. #saying#.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene lean_windows
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : #tallow.capitalize#'s dearer this month. Folk are going to bed with the hens. | Every window on the row is dark early. That's a lean time, plain as anything. | I've stopped buying new candles at all. #stubs.capitalize# will see me through.
b : It'll ease. | It is. | Lucky you saved.
a : Maybe. I'll keep saving #stubs# till it does. | It is. I'll put an end in the window anyway, for the look of it. | Not luck. #saying#.

scene end_cottage
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #stranger#'s come up the pass. I'll watch a while before I say anything. | There's a light on late in the end cottage. Somebody new. | A stranger asked me for a light. I gave a stub. I didn't give my name.
b : Wise. | Late, is it? | Fair enough.
a : Watching's free. Talking costs you, later. | Every night. I'd like to know what's worth the #tallow#. | A stub's cheap. A name's dearer. #tch#.

story dark_week [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : When I was a #child#, the lamp oil ran out in a hard winter, and we sat a week in the dark.
  : My #gran# found one candle end in a drawer. We lit it an hour a night and told stories by it.
  ask : And what would an hour of light be for, in your house?
  b : Stories, same as yours.
  b[old] : I remember winters like that. Every house had one.
  : I've never thrown an end away since. Not one.

story chandler_glass [topic=memories|dreams self.age>=20]
  : There was a chandler down the valley when I was a #child#, with candles hung in the window like icicles.
  : I'd stand with my nose on the glass till the old fellow came out and shooed me off.
  : One day, instead of shooing me, he gave me a broken one. I've still got it.
  b : That was kind of him.
  b[stage=young] : Can I see it?
  : Kind. And a mistake. That's how it started. #tch#.

dlg @3 resident.hub : #greet#. What's wanted? | #greet#, #address#. Say it; I'm listening.
dlg @4 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You'll know where the stool is. | #topic.player#. #good.capitalize#. Sit near the light.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=miner] : I dig, and I make my lamp last longer than anyone. Don't ask me how.
dlg @2 resident.job : #work.capitalize#, then home, then I save. That's as much as anyone needs. | Whatever pays, #address#. And it all goes in the same place.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# And I'd not be the one to spread it if there were. | Not a word I'd pass on, #address#.
dlg @2 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep to the lit side. | #farewell#, #address#. Take a stub for the lane.
graft resident.hub
choice What's in the jar on your shelf? -> end_jar
node end_jar
say Candle ends. Hundreds. Every one I've ever had, near enough. #tch#. You'll want to know why. Everyone does.
mood calm
free
choice Why save them? -> end_jar_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node end_jar_why
say Because six ends make a candle, and candles make a living. One day. That's all anyone gets from me. Here, take one. You'll need it on the pass.
mood pleased
choice Thank you. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet : #greet#. I found #stub# by the chapel. It's mine now. | #greet#, #address#. Mind your feet.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Mind where you tread; I've dropped something.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I'm going home before it's dark. | Bye. #farewell#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Bye, #address#.
line @1 react.news : Oh. I didn't know, #address#. I won't say I did. | #surprise#. I'll not tell anyone.
line @1 decline : No, thank you. I'd rather stay by #stub#, where it's light. | I'd better not, #address#. I'm meant to be home before dark, and I'd be scared anyway.
scene y_stub_jar
when topic=pastimes|home|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep candle ends in #jar#. Nobody knows how many. | I found #stub# under the chapel bench. Nobody saw me take it. | #jar.capitalize#'s nearly full. I counted twice, in the dark.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : What do you want them for? | That's thrift, that is. | In the dark?
b : How many? | Clever. | In the dark?
a@grown : #secret#. I'll tell you when I'm big. | #stubs.capitalize# don't count as stealing. I asked. | With my fingers. You can count by feel.
a : Lots. More than you'd think. #secret#. | I know. #tch#. | By feel. It's easy when you practise.

scene y_little_light
when topic=home|smalltalk here.time=dusk|night
does confide / reassure / assess
a : I sleep with #stub# lit in a saucer. Only a little one. | When the light goes out I hold my breath till somebody brings #stub#. | I don't like the dark. I keep #stub# in my pocket, in case.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Mind it doesn't tip over. | Breathe, little one. The dark's only dark. | That's sensible. Have you a flint?
b : Me neither, much. | Hold your breath? | Good idea.
a@grown : It's stood in water, all round. I thought of that. | I know. I hold it anyway. | Not yet. I'm saving for one. Nearly there.
a : We could share my stub. If you're careful with it. | Till my ears hurt. Then I breathe. | It is. I thought of it myself. #tch#.

scene y_oatcake
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I had #oatcake# and made it last a whole hour. Tiny bites. | I hid #oatcake# in my pocket for later. It's crumbs now. | I can eat three oatcakes. I've done it twice.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Tiny bites make it last. Clever. | Crumbs still count. | Three? You'll be sick.
b : A whole hour? | Crumbs are still food. | Three!
a@grown : I'm good at making things last. #tch#. | They do. I ate them off my paw. | I wasn't. Nearly, the second time.
a : Nearly. I counted. | They are. I ate every one. | Three. I could do four, if nobody looked, #address#.

scene y_mist
when topic=weather|day here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #mist.capitalize#'s that thick, the gate's gone. I'm staying in. | #mist.capitalize# ate the whole lane. I went to the well holding the wall. | I like #mist#. Nobody can see me in it.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : It'll lift by noon. | That's the way, along the wall. | Nobody can see you, so mind the carts.
b : Me too. | Holding the wall? | Hiding, are you?
a@grown : I'll wait. I'm good at waiting. | It's the only way I know where I am in #mist#. | I'll mind them. I'll hear them first.
a : We'll wait for it together. Quietly. | All the way. It was #cold#. | A bit. Don't tell anyone.

scene y_saving
when topic=dreams|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When I'm big I'll have a shop with a candle in every window. | I'm saving buttons. And #stubs#. Not telling you why. | I've got a coin. I'm not spending it. Ever, maybe.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : A chandler, then. That's a good trade. | Your secret's safe with me. | Saving's wise. Don't let it fall down a crack.
b : A whole shop! | Go on, tell me. | Ever?
a@grown : A chandler. I'll make my own candles from #stubs#. | It's still a secret. #tch#. | It's sewn in my sleeve. Nobody'll find it.
a : A whole shop. With a bell on the door. | No. #saying#. | Ever. Or till I've two.

rule @y_stub
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Another #stub#! That's mine. | Mind, you'll tread on it. That's a #good# end, that.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Folk I don't know, I'm to be careful of. Quickly, then. | #greet#, #address#. What is it?
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | Bye, #address#. Go home before it's dark.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#. I've a minute, no more.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. I'd wondered when you'd come by.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, then.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. That stays with me, I think. | Oh. News to me, and it goes no further, #address#.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, no. I've things to do that I'd rather not explain. | Not this time, #address#. I'm saving, and going out costs.
scene ad_dipping
when topic=pastimes|work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've started dipping my own candles from #stubs#. Lumpy, but they burn. | I melted down half #jar# last night. The whole house smelled of #tallow#. | Nobody taught me to dip. I watched through the chandler's window till I knew.
b : Lumpy's fine if it burns. | They'll have loved that. | Through the window?
a : It burns. Crooked, but it burns. #tch#. | They opened every shutter, #cold# or not. I'm not popular. | Every day for a month. I'd stand where the draught was warmest.

scene ad_box
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Folk keep asking what I'm saving for. I tell them a pair of boots. #tch#. | Somebody went through my things. Nothing's missing, but I know. | I keep a box under the floor. I'm only telling you it's there, not where.
b : And is it boots? | Who would do that? | Why tell me at all?
a : It's boots, if they ask again. #saying#. | #dunno.capitalize#. I've moved it all now, anyway. | So somebody knows, if I'm ever not here to say.

scene ad_learner
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm learning a trade, #address#. I keep my mouth shut and my eyes open. | I got told off for being slow. I wasn't slow; I was being careful. | They let me hold the light while they work. I watch everything.
b : That's how you learn. | There's a difference. | You'll be doing it soon.
a : It is. Nobody notices you if you're quiet. That's useful. | There is. I'll not argue it with them, though. #tch#. | Sooner than they think. I'll not tell them that.

rule @ad_draught
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Shut that door. The light's guttering. | #tch#. #draught.capitalize#. Every candle in the room's leaning.

story ad_lost_coin [topic=memories|smalltalk]
  : I lost a coin once, down a crack in the floorboards. I'd been saving it since the thaw.
  : I lay on the floor every night with #stub# lit, looking down that crack.
  ask : How long would you have kept looking?
  b : A week, maybe. Did you get it back?
  b[stage=young] : Forever!
  : A month. Then I prised the board up. It was there, and a second one beside it. I'm still not sorry. #tch#.

dlg @2 resident.hub : #greet#. Make it quick; I'm wanted at home. | #greet#, #address#. What's this about?
